 the nearest 50 cents  a lot of information is lost  we can do that  one of the things we'll do in the papers  we'll propose well if you want to  discretize here's a way to discretize  it's not actually just rounding to the  nearest 50 cents it's kind of doing a  discrete process that's centered at the  truth  and if you do it this way  then you can still get the causal  influence you want downstream  yeah maybe just take an opportunity with  this crowd that there's been a bit of a  breakthrough both at stanford and  michael's kind of business group ours  here on conformal prediction  so you can get uncertainty distribution  free  non-asymptotic and you don't need  independence you need exchangeability  and  i think a lot of what you're doing with  this kind of thing and conformal is  actually kind of like we have a private  prediction sets paper where we talk  about doing this with their program so  here you know i think a lot of  theoreticians would do if you haven't  looked at the check they want to because  it's there's a lot of open periodical  questions about it  uh thanks to all the fellows for uh  range of topics and thanks all for  coming and i hope to see all of you  after that  you

